  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "CMIP6 oxygen is stored per unit volume (mol m-3) while WOA23 oxygen and the 20/60 thresholds are in micromoles per kilogram, so the mass-per-volume conversion directly affects OMZ volumes and oxygen inventories.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Convert `o2` (mol m-3) to µmol kg-1 with the in-situ density (`compute_potential_density_anomaly` with `ref_pressure=None`; `transform_unit`'s constant surface default errs ~1% in the deep ocean and fresh polar water) before applying the 20 and 60 µmol kg-1 thresholds, and state the `attrs['density_assumption']` used.",
        "Inventories: integrate the native mol m-3 field with `convert_concentration_to_content` (Σ c · volcello, no density); feeding it a µmol kg-1 field applies the constant default and biases by ~1%."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-o2sat-and-derived-oxygen",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-o2sat-and-derived-oxygen.md",
      "sha256": "afe46747641c91aff8ddc9f50165a800a7c64d5d2e39b50e816280d02e59fba3",
      "reason": "WOA23 AOU and percent oxygen saturation within the OMZ depend on the AOU = o2sat − o2 definition and on observational solubility and mass-unit conventions, which also inform the respiration-versus-ventilation interpretation.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`identify_oxygen_minimum_zone` and any threshold comparison evaluate in the field's own units, so a mol m-3 `o2` field must be converted first or the whole ocean is flagged as below the threshold.",
        "WOA23 percent saturation and AOU rest on the WOA convention/pressure assumptions, not the OMIP (Garcia & Gordon 1992, 0.20946 O2 mole fraction, `P_a/P⁰_a`) recipe; treat model–WOA AOU or %sat differences as including a definitional component."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "CMIP6 land and below-sea-floor cells are marked with 1e20, so they must be masked before any OMZ volume or oxygen inventory sum or they will silently dominate the result.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Read 1e20 as NaN (default xarray decoding); a value near 1e20 in output is an unmasked fill. Build each field's valid mask from the field itself — masks differ between variables of the same model — and mask the weights (volcello/areacello) to the same cells.",
        "Use `compute_exceedance_fraction` for the below-threshold volumes: it keeps missing cells out of both numerator and denominator."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "volcello and areacello provide tracer-cell volume and recoverable layer thickness, which are required for OMZ volume and summed OMZ thickness in a column using the models’ own grids.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The archive has no `thkcello`/`masscello`: take column thickness as volcello/areacello (`cell_thickness_like`), not the `lev_bnds` difference, which fails at partial bottom cells (14% of GFDL-ESM4 cells differ >1%).",
        "Use `deptho` (model bathymetry) or the field's own fill pattern, not external topography, to decide whether a level is above the sea floor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "OMZ volumes and dissolved oxygen inventories should be integrated on the native grids because regridding changes the land-sea mask and breaks conservation; regridding is appropriate for the maps.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute every number (OMZ volumes, basin volumes, inventory, max thickness) on each source's native grid with its own weights; regrid to the WOA 1° grid only for the Figure 1/2 maps, and build one shared mask before cell-by-cell statistics.",
        "Do not vertically interpolate for OMZ thickness: integrate thickness on the original levels (`regrid_vertical` would change layer-integrated quantities); interpolation to fixed depths is for comparison only."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The global oxygen inventory and basin OMZ volumes are volume-weighted integrals over every ocean grid cell in the region, not simple unweighted cell averages or subsampled sums.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Volume-weight every mean and integral: OMZ volume is Σ volcello over valid cells below the threshold (a share of volume, not of cells); Pacific/Indian/Atlantic volumes apply the basin mask on the model's own grid.",
        "For a map-wide statistic (RMSE, bias, pattern correlation against WOA) weight by area: `compute_difference_metrics` does by default, `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "The CMIP6 oxygen fields are monthly time averages, and applying the 20/60 threshold is a nonlinear diagnostic, so OMZ volume computed from monthly means differs from the mean of monthly OMZ volumes and must be stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "f(monthly mean) ≠ mean of f: oxygen-threshold volumes and AOU from monthly means depend on order; state whether the diagnostic was formed first or the mean state first (WOA is a climatology, so average-then-diagnose is the like-for-like choice).",
        "Average a period with `temporal_aggregate` (day weights in the model calendar); plain `compute_basic_stat(op='mean', dim='time')` weights months equally and is not a time average."
      ]
    },
